{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateFSTrichotomy"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.screen_out_selfDual_candidate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.screen_out_selfDual_candidate","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SelfDualSectorConfinement.lean#L181-L188","doc":"The contrapositive as a screening test: a candidate whose irreps are all\nself-dual is dead at dimension three, and no further analysis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.self_duality_is_the_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.self_duality_is_the_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SelfDualSectorConfinement.lean#L161-L179","doc":"**The specification for Route A.**  The two halves together.\n\n*Necessity*: any object of dimension `3` that passes must contain a\ncomplex-type irrep (`gate_forces_complex_of_dim_three`).\n*The single-fibre failure*: a category all of whose objects are self-dual\ncontains none, and so reaches no such object.\n\nSo the property a groupoid construction must exhibit is exactly the property a\nsingle `SU(2)` fibre lacks.  A candidate can be tested by asking whether its\nthree-dimensional object is isomorphic to its own dual, before any `Sym²`\ndecomposition is attempted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.single_fibre_su2_excludes_dim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.single_fibre_su2_excludes_dim_three","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SelfDualSectorConfinement.lean#L143-L157","doc":"**The single-fibre case.**  `SU(2)` has no complex-type irrep — every one is\nself-dual, real for integer and quaternionic for half-integer spin — so the\nhypothesis of the previous theorem is satisfied outright and the single-fibre\ntower cannot host a three-dimensional object that passes.\n\nThe `SU(2)` fact is the cited input (`[fulton-harris1991]` §3.5), carried here\nas the hypothesis `hsu2` rather than assumed silently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.selfDual_category_excludes_dim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SelfDualSectorConfinement.selfDual_category_excludes_dim_three","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SelfDualSectorConfinement.lean#L126-L141","doc":"**The confinement, correctly premised.**  In a category where every\noccurring irrep is self-dual, no object of dimension `3` passes the `Sym²`\ngate.\n\nThis is what `eightfold-open-problems.md` §1 needs.  The self-duality\nhypothesis is doing the work; without it the statement is false, by\n`Sym2GateComplexType.complex_three_passes_gate`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}